Additional Use Grant:

The following production uses of the Licensed Work are permitted free of charge
until the Change Date:

1. Production use by individuals, commercial entities, and other for-profit
   organizations whose Commercial Scale did not exceed USD 5,000,000 as of the
   end of their most recently completed fiscal year.
2. Production use by non-profit organizations, non-governmental organizations
   (NGOs), registered non-profit associations, and state-recognized educational
   institutions.
3. Production use by government authorities of countries classified as a
   "Low Income Economy" by the World Bank.
4. Listing, indexing, packaging, and including the Licensed Work in software
   catalogs, app catalogs, package indexes, deployment templates, one-click
   installers, documentation, integration guides, discovery services, and
   substantially similar directories, provided that the listing or inclusion is
   not sold as a paid Nebulynk-specific commercial offering and the third party
   does not sell, rent, host, operate, manage, or provide paid
   Nebulynk-specific services or paid Nebulynk-specific placement without a
   prior written partnership agreement or commercial license from the Licensor.
5. Deployment facilitation by third parties, including automated provisioning,
   deployment templates, one-click installers, update automation, and
   pass-through or marked-up infrastructure billing, provided that:
   a. the customer remains responsible for selecting, paying for, and
      controlling the underlying infrastructure or account, or the
      infrastructure charge is itemized separately;
   b. any markup, platform fee, or automation fee is charged as a general
      cloud, infrastructure, or deployment-platform fee and is not priced per
      Nebulynk user, seat, workspace, tenant, message, feature, or other
      Nebulynk-specific usage metric;
   c. the third party does not market the offering as official Nebulynk,
      Nebulynk Cloud, Managed Nebulynk, or a substantially similar
      Nebulynk-specific hosted or managed service; and
   d. the third party does not provide Nebulynk-specific paid support,
      operations, administration, service-level commitments, backups,
      monitoring, or incident response without a prior written partnership
      agreement or commercial license from the Licensor.

A general infrastructure markup or general platform fee does not by itself make
an offering a prohibited commercial Nebulynk-specific service.

Non-production use, including testing, development, staging, evaluation,
security research, internal proof-of-concept work, and demonstrations, is free
of charge for all users.

For purposes of this Additional Use Grant, "Commercial Scale" means the highest
of gross revenue, total operating budget, or cumulative funding and investments
received by the user and its Affiliates. "Affiliate" means any entity that
directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control
with the user. Control means ownership of more than 50% of voting power or the
practical ability to direct management or business decisions.

Amounts reported in a currency other than USD must be converted using the
exchange rate used in the user's audited or formally approved financial
statements for the relevant fiscal year. If no such rate is available, use the
average daily exchange rate for that fiscal year published by the U.S. Federal
Reserve. If that rate is unavailable, use the European Central Bank reference
rate for the relevant period.

If a user qualified for free production use at the beginning of a fiscal year
but reasonably determines during that fiscal year that its Commercial Scale has
exceeded USD 5,000,000, the user may continue production use only if it obtains
a commercial license for that fiscal year or stops production use within
90 days. For the fiscal year in which the threshold is first exceeded, the
Licensor's standard annual license fee will be reduced by 50% for a commercial
license covering that year. This reduction applies only once per user and its
Affiliates.

No Additional Use Grant is made for offering the Licensed Work, modified
versions, or derivative works as a hosted, managed, or substantially similar
network service to third parties when that offering has a commercial character,
including as part of paid SaaS, managed hosting, paid operations, reseller,
marketplace, or platform services. Such use requires a prior written partnership
agreement or commercial license from the Licensor. This paragraph does not
limit catalog, package, directory, deployment-template inclusion, or deployment
facilitation permitted under items 4 or 5 above.

